The selector mock was never matched because the `getSObjectType()` stub was removed in my last revision. `Application.Selector.setMock` registers the mock under `getSObjectType()`. Without that stub the lookup returned null, so `OpportunitiesSelector.newInstance()` fell through to the real selector and returned no rows. I restored the stub through the `fflib_ISObjectSelector` base type, which avoids the compile error from the `IOpportunitiesSelector` reference.

