The tests returned empty maps because `Application.Selector` never handed back the mock. `fflib_Application.SelectorFactory.setMock` routes by the mock's `getSObjectType()`, and an unstubbed mock returns null, so `newInstance(Opportunity.SObjectType)` fell through to the real selector. The fix is to stub `getSObjectType()` to return `Opportunity.SObjectType` in each test. I also replaced the `null` verify argument with typed variables to avoid the earlier ambiguous-overload compile error.

